  "description": "Titanium road frame, made to order in Somerset.The Fosse is the culmination of hundreds of custom builds for our clients, distilled into a single, highly versatile road frame. Six sizes, each in three stack heights offer the chance to fine tune the fit for speed and performance but its core focus is for longer, endurance-friendly riding. A relatively low bottom bracket offsets the wider tyres now common on road builds, keeping it stable at speed without losing the agility you’d expect of a road bike. Finding your ideal fit is simple with our comprehensive fitting tools. The Fosse showcases the latest engineering and manufacturing developments from Sturdy Cycles. We have replaced our 3D-printed junctions and components with fully redesigned, CNC-machined titanium alternatives, machined in-house and built to order at our Frome workshop. This new manufacturing approach brings a sharp, modern and minimal look, so every Sturdy remains a unique proposition: truly functional UK engineering, refined with handmade finesse.Road grime and winter spray find their way into everything, so we’ve placed phosphor-bronze threads at the thru-axles and seatpost clamp, and each frame kit includes an Enduro headset backed by a lifetime bearing warranty. Paired with the included ENVE IN-Route Road carbon fork, the frame kit takes tyres up to 700×35mm. An optional titanium fork, launching in 2027, expands clearance to 38mm. Every frame kit also comes complete with an in-house CNC-machined titanium stem and seatpost. Customise your build with optional custom finishing, a complete 1X or 2X build kit, and our titanium crankset or accessory bundles.Fosse Way: the Roman road that ran from Exeter to Lincoln, built in the first century AD. It still cuts an almost straight line across Somerset, a few miles from our Frome workshop.",
